From cd25a618184c2b176a016712393f6b1c1315f198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:53:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: add ds_resolve to resolve depth/stencil inside
 stitched passes

MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=ds_resolve resolves depth and stencil attachments of
stitched render passes with the render pass itself, instead of with meta
passes afterwards, also when the render area is smaller than the
framebuffer but starts at the origin. The queue wait after stitched
passes orders the resolve before later work. The resolve texture is set
in every segment so their descriptors stay equal, and the legacy custom
resolve path, which reads the multisampled depth, still stores it and
resolves afterwards.

When a partial render target is both stored and resolved, Metal does not
resolve layers after the first, so a don't-care depth or stencil
attachment resolved in the pass is not force-stored at the end of the
pass. Metal then also writes the resolve texture outside the render area.

KK_DUMP_RESOLVE_DIR also writes the resolved depth.

